# Host-local plaintext credentials. Copy this example only when secret.env is missing.
# Supply values locally; never commit secret.env or paste its contents into chat.
# docs/host-secrets.md owns setup, selected-action requirements and native account auth.

# Supply an existing shared age identity locally. Initial identity publication has its own setup owner.
# Keep this commented when no identity has been supplied; an active blank intentionally disables it.
# SOPS_AGE_KEY=

# SonarCloud analyses everything that lives in the runtime repository (the runtime and the three examples): the release cut's Sonar proof reads the token.
# SONAR_TOKEN: sonarcloud.io > My Account > Security > Generate Tokens (the same token is the repository secret SONAR_TOKEN).
# The organization key is configuration, not a secret: config.yaml `sonar: {organization: <key>}` (or the environment variable SONAR_ORGANIZATION).
SONAR_TOKEN=
# A product repository scanned on the self-hosted server (ext/sonar) supplies its own SONAR_TOKEN and SONAR_HOST_URL in its own environment; a host is declared, not a secret.
# Not for SonarCloud: the stack's own names are the SONARQUBE_* ones below.
# The self-hosted Sonar stack of product repositories (ext/sonar, README there) takes its secrets from here; `starci gate sonar up` passes them to Compose.
# SONARQUBE_DB_PASSWORD: the database password of the stack (any strong value; set it before the first start, a running database keeps the one it was created with).
# SONARQUBE_ADMIN_PASSWORD: the admin password the stack's bootstrap sets in place of SonarQube's default.
# SONARQUBE_ADMIN_TOKEN: a SonarQube user token of that admin (My Account > Security); sonar-local.mjs provisions product projects with it.
# SONARQUBE_DB_PASSWORD=
# SONARQUBE_ADMIN_PASSWORD=
# SONARQUBE_ADMIN_TOKEN=
# Only a selected remotely managed tunnel uses this token: `starci gate sonar up --public`, and the connector tunnel of config.yaml cloudflare.tokenEnv.
# CLOUDFLARE_TUNNEL_TOKEN=
# Only an enabled Telegram connector uses this token.
# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
